WEBVTT

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:02.482
Hi, I'm Confetti!

00:00:02.482 --> 00:00:06.852
Limite 1B Violetto is a small maths model sold as high-throughput.

00:00:06.852 --> 00:00:08.442
Its config shows why.

00:00:10.183 --> 00:00:13.960
Three blocks in four look back only a thousand and twenty-four tokens.

00:00:13.960 --> 00:00:16.478
Just twelve of forty-eight keep a growing cache.

00:00:20.733 --> 00:00:24.622
Most parts read like a speedrun changelog, and cost nothing at inference.

00:00:25.042 --> 00:00:29.684
A second embedding table feeds sixteen blocks' value path straight from the token id.

00:00:30.105 --> 00:00:34.033
Two dense shortcuts, at half-way and the exit, reach back to earlier blocks.

00:00:34.453 --> 00:00:37.818
Norms have no learnable gain, and the attention scale is pinned

00:00:37.818 --> 00:00:39.042
at zero point one.

00:00:40.333 --> 00:00:44.349
A windowed block looks back a thousand and twenty-four tokens, with short

00:00:44.349 --> 00:00:46.357
rotary positions on half its channels.

00:00:46.777 --> 00:00:50.825
Every fourth block is global: it sees everything, with no positions at all.

00:00:52.108 --> 00:00:53.697
What does one token cost a block?

00:00:54.117 --> 00:00:56.301
Keys and values, for two KV heads.

00:00:56.301 --> 00:00:57.862
Ten query heads share them.

00:00:58.282 --> 00:01:01.554
Each head is a hundred and twenty-eight wide, two bytes a number.

00:01:01.974 --> 00:01:03.760
A thousand and twenty-four bytes.

00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:08.045
At a hundred and thirty-one thousand tokens, a global block holds a

00:01:08.045 --> 00:01:11.259
hundred and thirty-four megabytes; a windowed one, about one.

00:01:12.925 --> 00:01:17.178
One point six five gigabytes in all, not six point four four.

00:01:17.178 --> 00:01:20.722
An eighty gigabyte card fits forty-four long problems, not eleven.

00:01:22.258 --> 00:01:25.280
The release's headline chart is about maths, not speed.

00:01:25.280 --> 00:01:29.308
Violetto is the purple dot, far left of models scoring the same.

00:01:29.728 --> 00:01:34.706
Its footnote: reinforcement learning is excluded, and counted stages differ by model.

00:01:36.017 --> 00:01:39.909
High throughput here means concurrency: forty-four long problems, not eleven.

00:01:39.909 --> 00:01:43.022
A ceiling from the config, not a measurement.

00:01:45.150 --> 00:01:49.319
Windowed blocks, a few global ones without positions, and a much smaller cache.

00:01:49.750 --> 00:01:51.912
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:51.912 --> 00:01:52.530
I'm Confetti.

00:01:52.530 --> 00:01:52.839
Bye!
